    "Conclusion: Business Value & Real-World Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "#Simulated ROI & Financial Impact\n",
    "Based on standard industry cost parameters for a 1,000-head barn, this predictive model demonstrates significant commercial viability:\n",
    "Reduced Mortality: Early detection of intake drop-offs enables immediate medical intervention, projecting a decrease in mortality rate from 3% to 0.5%.\n",
    "*Resource Protection: Immediate flagging of mechanical anomalies stops catastrophic water leaks on Day 1.\n",
    "*Bottom Line: The model projects $3,000 in net profit protection per barn, annually, delivering an estimated 200% Return on Investment (ROI)on standard IoT sensor infrastructure.\n",
    "\n",
    "Real-World Considerations (Future Work)\n",
    "While the simulated financial models represent optimal conditions, deploying this pipeline in a physical barn requires handling messy data:\n",
    "1. Sensor Reliability: Real-world data features missing values due to power outages, chewed wires, or clogged water meters. Future models must handle `NaN` inputs robustly.\n",
    "2. Alert Fatigue: Routine farm activities (like pen washdowns) can trigger false \"leak\" alerts. A production model would require a tiered alert system or contextual flags (e.g., a \"Wash Mode\" button for staff) to prevent farm managers from ignoring the system."
